  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Alkene hydrogenation is the syn-addition of hydrogen to an alkene, saturating the bond.</p><p>A compound capable of optical rotation is said to be optically active. For a compound to be optically active, it should contain chiral carbon.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0022_8dfc0e36fe08.jpg\"/><br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\st0022_d451f6811c33.jpg\"/></p>"
